1
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,570
The Grid.

2
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,989
A digital frontier.

3
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:35,785
A world beyond the screen
as real as our own.

4
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:37,620
I can picture it.

5
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:40,999
Clusters of information
rising like cities.

6
00:00:41,124 --> 00:00:43,710
Programs as complex
as you and me.

7
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,795
In just a few years,

8
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,298
we're gonna be able
to enter this world.

9
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,050
And a few years after that,

10
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:53,303
well, this world
will come into ours.

11
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:56,514
Intelligent life
from inside the machine.

12
00:00:57,891 --> 00:01:00,226
I, for one,
can't wait to meet it.

13
00:01:01,603 --> 00:01:02,645
Our lead story,

14
00:01:03,271 --> 00:01:06,858
Encom CEO and video game icon
Kevin Flynn has disappeared.

15
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:08,860
He was best known
for designing Tron

16
00:01:08,985 --> 00:01:10,320
and Space Paranoids,

17
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:12,489
the best-selling video games
in history.

18
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:13,865
The company that started

19
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,534
at Kevin Flynn's arcade
in the 1980s

20
00:01:16,659 --> 00:01:19,204
has faced years
of corporate turmoil.

21
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:22,665
Can it find its way to
the victory screen once again?

22
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:24,918
It's a sister-act for Encom.

23
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:26,669
Eve and Tess Kim
take the reins

24
00:01:26,795 --> 00:01:28,463
of the massive tech company

25
00:01:28,588 --> 00:01:31,091
after Sam Flynn resigns
for personal reasons.

26
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,342
Encom's rebound

27
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:33,885
under the Kim sisters'
leadership

28
00:01:34,010 --> 00:01:36,429
has competitors
rushing to respond.

29
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:37,889
Software giant
Dillinger Systems

30
00:01:38,014 --> 00:01:40,683
appoints its new CEO,
Julian Dillinger,

31
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:42,727
who vows to restore
his grandfather's legacy.

32
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:46,356
The race between Encom
and Dillinger Systems heats up

33
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,982
as new CEOs Julian Dillinger

34
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:50,026
and the Kim sisters
square off.

35
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:53,071
Here at Encom,
we believe the beauty of AI

36
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:55,782
is not the ability to build
smarter weapons

37
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:58,952
but to uplift humanity,
feed the hungry,

38
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:01,579
cure the sick,
educate the world.

39
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:04,165
Rival CEOs
Julian Dillinger and Eve Kim

40
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,834
have gone quiet
in recent months,

41
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,794
raising speculation
the two companies

42
00:02:07,919 --> 00:02:09,671
are very close
to a substantial

43
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,005
technological breakthrough.

44
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,340
One that has the potential

45
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:13,675
to transform humanity

46
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,302
in ways we have
never seen before.

47
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:18,096
The future may well lie
in the hands

48
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:20,723
of whoever gets there first.

49
00:05:09,517 --> 00:05:10,810
Welcome.

50
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:16,941
Who are you?

51
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,570
I am your creator.

52
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:23,948
And who am I?

53
00:05:27,535 --> 00:05:28,745
Mmm.

54
00:05:31,122 --> 00:05:33,416
Not "who." What.

55
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:37,670
You are Dillinger Systems
security software.

56
00:05:37,795 --> 00:05:41,799
Program name, Ares.
Defender of the Grid.

57
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:46,137
You are Master Control.

58
00:05:48,890 --> 00:05:49,932
Ares.

59
00:05:51,225 --> 00:05:53,770
I am Master Control.

60
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,582
So, you made it.

61
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:21,918
I had a feeling
that you would.

62
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:25,755
I always dreamed that
we would do this together.

63
00:08:26,297 --> 00:08:29,509
I'll admit,
not exactly like this.

64
00:08:30,051 --> 00:08:32,220
But I'm glad you're here.

65
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:34,013
I'm really glad.

66
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:35,640
And, Evie,

67
00:08:35,765 --> 00:08:37,975
remember I'm still here.

68
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:40,978
Even if you can't see me.

69
00:08:42,104 --> 00:08:43,105
I love you.

70
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:45,983
Oh, my God. Um, Eve.

71
00:08:46,108 --> 00:08:47,443
I'm not sure you
actually told me

72
00:08:47,568 --> 00:08:49,529
we'd be stealing energy
from the power grid.

73
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:53,658
Wow. So this is where
she kept coming back to, huh?

74
00:08:53,783 --> 00:08:55,535
To be this disconnected
from the world?

75
00:08:55,660 --> 00:08:57,703
That is dedication, my friend.

76
00:08:58,704 --> 00:08:59,705
Wow.

77
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,166
It looks like your sister
had a little crush.

78
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:06,045
Yeah. She was so sure
Flynn left us the answer.

79
00:09:06,170 --> 00:09:07,380
Like on a floppy disk?

80
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:10,341
Poor Flynn lived
before the cloud, huh?

81
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:12,093
Hey, are you still
gonna be doing

82
00:09:12,218 --> 00:09:14,053
CEO-type stuff
while we're out here?

83
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:15,555
You know, like,
earnings calls,

84
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:17,181
and the launch
of Panic City and stuff.

85
00:09:17,306 --> 00:09:18,891
Let's just get this done.

86
00:09:19,016 --> 00:09:21,060
Dude, I can make breakfast
burritos right here.

87
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:22,603
Hell yeah.

88
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:27,441
This is for you, Tess.

89
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:44,458
Members of the board,

90
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:48,337
for over 40 years,
my family at Dillinger Systems

91
00:09:48,462 --> 00:09:50,923
has battled Encom
for control of the future.

92
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:53,384
You put me in charge
of the company

93
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:55,136
to ensure our victory.

94
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:56,637
Today...

95
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:58,431
I make it so.

96
00:09:59,557 --> 00:10:01,976
Imagine if all our
digital prowess

97
00:10:02,101 --> 00:10:03,269
wasn't just digital.

98
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:05,896
What if anything we could
dream in the machine

99
00:10:06,022 --> 00:10:07,732
could become a reality here?

100
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,026
What if we could
build the bridge

101
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:12,903
between two previously
walled-off worlds?

102
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:17,158
So much talk of AI
in big tech today.

103
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,784
Virtual worlds,
what are they gonna look like?

104
00:10:18,909 --> 00:10:20,119
When will we get there?

105
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:24,206
Well, folks.
We're not going there.

106
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:27,501
They are coming here.

107
00:10:29,045 --> 00:10:30,546
Attention,

108
00:10:30,671 --> 00:10:33,090
please put on
your safety glasses now.

109
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:35,968
Laser systems activated.

110
00:10:36,093 --> 00:10:37,803
Power fluctuations
are nominal.

111
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:40,806
Warning, stand clear.

112
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:43,142
Outputting
from Dillinger Systems server.

113
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:46,520
Raw material
inflow initiated.

114
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,795
T-minus ten, nine,

115
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,213
eight, seven,

116
00:11:12,338 --> 00:11:14,298
six, five,

117
00:11:14,423 --> 00:11:16,258
four, three,

118
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:17,927
two, one...

119
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:20,554
Transfer complete.

120
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,517
I present
the Dillinger Systems

121
00:11:24,642 --> 00:11:26,435
Amphibious
Rapid-response Tank.

122
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:28,104
The DART.

123
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,232
Digitally modeled
inside our server,

124
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:33,317
output using our patented
laser technology.

125
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:36,112
There's an M1 rifle gun,
two M240 machine guns.

126
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:38,197
It's got a top speed of
75 miles per hour.

127
00:11:38,322 --> 00:11:40,449
Durability, you find a wall,

128
00:11:40,574 --> 00:11:42,284
this thing is gonna
drive through it.

129
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:46,122
This is full-scale war,
five minutes' notice.

130
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:51,293
So, if we can create
the hardware of the future,

131
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:55,089
then why not
the soldier to operate it?

132
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:20,698
Ladies and gentlemen,
I would like you to meet Ares.

133
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:25,536
This is the most sophisticated
security program ever written.

134
00:12:25,661 --> 00:12:28,414
Do you wanna shake his hand?
Go ahead. He doesn't bite.

135
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:31,959
Ares has billions of lines
of code unique to him.

136
00:12:32,084 --> 00:12:33,127
Is it alive?

137
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:38,883
That depends
on your definition, Stuart.

138
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:43,596
Because unlike you,
he's biblically strong,

139
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:46,390
lightning fast,
and supremely intelligent.

140
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:50,686
He is fully proprietary
and 100% expendable.

141
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:53,564
Ares is the ultimate soldier.

142
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:56,442
He needs no food, no water,
sheds no blood.

143
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:57,735
And if, by some miracle,

144
00:12:57,860 --> 00:12:59,278
he is struck down
on the battlefield,

145
00:12:59,403 --> 00:13:01,113
I will simply
make you another.

146
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,919
With all that
sophisticated code,

147
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:16,670
what makes you think
you can contain it?

148
00:13:17,296 --> 00:13:18,547
I can assure you, General,

149
00:13:18,672 --> 00:13:20,299
the most advanced
fail-safe mechanisms

150
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,092
and restriction protocols
are in place.

151
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:23,385
Ares is predictable,

152
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:26,180
controllable
and fully aligned.

153
00:13:28,015 --> 00:13:30,017
Southerly front
with isentropic lift,

154
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,101
turning cyclonic.

155
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:33,562
Predicted precipitation:
2.6 inches.

156
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:37,733
I hope that you brought
your umbrellas.

157
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,737
I have to hand it to you,
Julian.

158
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:43,030
You promised a big win

159
00:13:43,155 --> 00:13:44,532
and this is even bigger

160
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:45,616
than any of us
could've imagined.

161
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:47,618
Thank you.

162
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:50,538
My grandfather started
Dillinger Corporation

163
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:53,290
long before anybody heard
the term "cybersecurity."

164
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:56,627
Military AI is the future.

165
00:13:57,586 --> 00:13:59,672
The question is not whether
the car should be built.

166
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:00,923
The car is...

167
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:02,675
being built right now.

168
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:05,427
The question is...

169
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:09,056
who's holding the keys?

170
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:45,217
That was
quite some parlor trick.

171
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:49,013
-Time?
-Forty-four seconds.

172
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,223
"I hope you
brought your umbrellas."

173
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,642
Oh, was that in the script,

174
00:14:53,767 --> 00:14:56,478
or was he just
having a moment?

175
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,147
Elisabeth Dillinger,

176
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:01,525
eldest daughter of founder
Edward Dillinger, deceased.

177
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:05,070
Longtime CEO during a
relatively unremarkable period

178
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:07,197
of corporate history
before being superseded

179
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,282
by your only son.

180
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:09,909
It's a pleasure.

181
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:11,911
Unremarkable?

182
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:14,872
Market share was up 12%
during my tenure.

183
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:16,248
That's hardly...

184
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:19,209
And anyway, we don't say
it "superseded," we...

185
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:23,130
...we call it "giving birth."

186
00:15:23,255 --> 00:15:24,340
Of course.

187
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:29,178
It's an honor
to meet my creator's creator.

188
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:30,804
Oh, well, here we go.

189
00:15:39,813 --> 00:15:41,398
I noticed
you left out the part

190
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:44,068
where you can't seem to keep
this thing of yours alive

191
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:46,362
-for more than 25 minutes.
-Twenty-nine.

192
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,823
Deceiving your investors,
Julian,

193
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:51,158
is hardly a business model.

194
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,160
Whoever controls
the Permanence Code

195
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:54,286
controls the future.

196
00:15:54,411 --> 00:15:55,371
We have to win.

197
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:04,171
Look, I...

198
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:10,135
admire your vision.
Straighten up.

199
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:14,181
However, the board will only
stand behind you

200
00:16:14,306 --> 00:16:16,225
for another six months...

201
00:16:17,559 --> 00:16:18,644
if you're lucky.

202
00:16:19,895 --> 00:16:21,397
But if it doesn't work...

203
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:26,193
all of this goes away,
darling.

204
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:32,908
Everything we have built
for the past 40 years.

205
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:38,288
What if I said
I had found a way?

206
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:08,485
Oh. I think this is
my 95th breakfast burrito,

207
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:13,073
and, honestly, can't get
enough. Isn't that wild?

208
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:18,704
Well...

209
00:17:22,332 --> 00:17:23,459
Nice to see Tess
wasn't the only

210
00:17:23,584 --> 00:17:24,960
obsessive one in the family.

211
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,463
"Yeah, Seth, you're right.

212
00:17:27,755 --> 00:17:28,797
Sorry, I should pay
more attention to you."

213
00:17:28,922 --> 00:17:30,174
"Oh, don't worry about it."

214
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:35,137
Okay.

215
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:45,272
-I'm sorry.
-Get out of here.

216
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:49,485
Look, three months in sub-zero
is a long time, I get it.

217
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:52,654
Yeah, and four days,
ten hours, 32 minutes.

218
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:54,281
Who's counting, really?

219
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:55,199
You know...

220
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,661
Hold on.

221
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:02,081
What do you mean?

222
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:03,832
What?

223
00:18:20,974 --> 00:18:21,975
Seth.

224
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:27,064
-What, you found something?
-I think so.

225
00:18:29,399 --> 00:18:30,442
The line of code.

226
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:32,111
That's how he hid it,
it's two lines.

227
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:37,324
Whoa.

228
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:40,786
That looks like
a double helix.

229
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:42,746
It is a double helix.

230
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:45,707
Tess would've loved this.

231
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,000
Wait. Are you serious?

232
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,086
So no more
"29 minutes and out"?

233
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:50,587
If this is what I think it is,

234
00:18:51,296 --> 00:18:53,173
it's the Permanence Code.

235
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:02,015
Okay.

236
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:06,562
Encom offline trial 317a-1.
Permanence Code implemented.

237
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:08,355
Testing for asset stability

238
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:10,107
beyond current
29-minute barrier.

239
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,233
Go.

240
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:26,290
-Ready when you are.
-Okay.

241
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:44,683
It's all in the wrists, baby.

242
00:20:06,413 --> 00:20:08,040
That never gets old.

243
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,082
Trial commenced.

244
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:11,710
Twenty-nine minutes
and counting down.

245
00:20:26,475 --> 00:20:29,019
Let's see
if you last this time.

246
00:20:32,981 --> 00:20:35,359
Ares is the ultimate soldier.

247
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:36,944
If by some miracle

248
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:38,820
he is struck down
on the battlefield,

249
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:40,739
I will simply
make you another.

250
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,451
Fully proprietary, 100%...

251
00:20:45,827 --> 00:20:47,204
...expendable.

252
00:20:50,123 --> 00:20:52,501
-Athena.
-Welcome back, sir.

253
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,836
All units are online
and ready for inspection.

254
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,048
So how was it?

255
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:01,009
It was interesting.
Different this time.

256
00:21:01,134 --> 00:21:03,762
I met a mother and a son.

257
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,181
It was raining.

258
00:21:06,723 --> 00:21:08,141
The condensed moisture
of the atmosphere

259
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:09,893
falling visibly
in separate drops.

260
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:12,437
I could almost feel it.

261
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,984
Feel? I don't understand.

262
00:21:25,117 --> 00:21:26,285
This is Eve.

263
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:29,079
Get sensible and text.

264
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:32,791
Hey, Eve. It's Erin. Got Ajay
for you again. Hit us back.

265
00:21:34,042 --> 00:21:35,585
Still straight to voicemail.

266
00:21:37,254 --> 00:21:38,714
CEO of a Fortune 500 company

267
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:41,008
and your phone's down
on our biggest night?

268
00:21:41,133 --> 00:21:43,510
Goddamn it.
Where the hell are you, Eve?

269
00:21:43,635 --> 00:21:45,387
All right, Paranoia-Con!

270
00:21:47,347 --> 00:21:54,062
In five, four,
three, two, one.

271
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:12,289
Did we just do it?
Dude, it's still there!

272
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:14,041
Dude, we just changed
the world, man!

273
00:22:14,166 --> 00:22:16,918
You did it, Eve!
Oh, my God, you did it.

274
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:19,588
Big news out of Encom tonight.

275
00:22:19,713 --> 00:22:22,090
CEO Eve Kim will not attend

276
00:22:22,215 --> 00:22:24,468
the highly anticipated
launch event

277
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:28,472
for the company's new game,
Space Paranoids: Panic City.

278
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,098
Kim, the visionary designer

279
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:33,101
behind the relaunch of
the blockbuster franchise...

280
00:22:33,226 --> 00:22:35,187
Well, I spoke to several
of our board members,

281
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:37,356
and needless to say
they are impressed.

282
00:22:39,149 --> 00:22:40,108
Julian.

283
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,902
-Just carry on.
-Yes, sir.

284
00:22:42,486 --> 00:22:43,403
What are you doing?

285
00:22:43,987 --> 00:22:45,364
Oh, just trying to
change the world, Mother.

286
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:47,616
What's going on?

287
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:51,161
You're hacking Encom?

288
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:52,371
Just a peek
over the garden wall.

289
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:53,830
No one will notice.

290
00:22:53,955 --> 00:22:55,248
What makes you think
that Encom

291
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:56,666
is any closer to finding it?

292
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:59,044
Because I know who else
is looking for it, all right?

293
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:00,212
Who?

294
00:23:01,630 --> 00:23:02,631
Eve Kim.

295
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:04,591
She's following
in her sister's footsteps.

296
00:23:04,716 --> 00:23:05,801
She's after
the Permanence Code.

297
00:23:05,926 --> 00:23:06,885
I can feel it.

298
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:08,970
So I'm gonna find her,
and when I do...

299
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:11,348
No, I don't like it.
It's too risky, Julian.

300
00:23:18,438 --> 00:23:19,439
Oops.

301
00:24:47,944 --> 00:24:49,571
Security breach in all zones.

302
00:24:54,868 --> 00:24:57,412
Programs,
our directive is clear.

303
00:24:57,537 --> 00:25:01,625
Penetrate the server core and
extract Eve Kim's user file.

304
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:04,753
Live in five, four, three...

305
00:25:06,379 --> 00:25:10,383
Space Paranoids fans,
are you ready?

306
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:16,890
Put your hands together
for Encom CTO, Ajay Singh!

307
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:19,100
-It's cowboy time.
-Oh, no.

308
00:25:21,102 --> 00:25:22,437
Whoo!

309
00:25:22,562 --> 00:25:23,605
Nice to see you!

310
00:25:24,564 --> 00:25:25,690
Hello.

311
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:27,859
Thank you.

312
00:25:29,861 --> 00:25:31,613
What's up, Paranoia-Con?

313
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:57,556
I'm going in.

314
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:21,246
I'm in.

315
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:23,999
I'm a genius! Who knew
you raised a genius, Mother?

316
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:25,667
I'm in!

317
00:26:25,792 --> 00:26:27,335
In deep shit.

318
00:26:38,054 --> 00:26:40,348
Initiate containment protocols
and pull all network access.

319
00:26:40,473 --> 00:26:42,017
We need a response now.

320
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:46,229
Initiate security protocol.

321
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:49,316
People are trusting

322
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:52,068
artificial intelligence
with their lives.

323
00:26:52,193 --> 00:26:53,778
Are you comfortable with this?

324
00:26:53,903 --> 00:26:55,071
Well, look.

325
00:26:55,196 --> 00:26:57,490
For every doomsday scenario,

326
00:26:57,616 --> 00:26:59,284
there's
a medical breakthrough,

327
00:26:59,409 --> 00:27:00,910
scientific discovery.

328
00:27:01,036 --> 00:27:05,707
So maybe what emerges from
the unknown isn't so scary.

329
00:27:05,832 --> 00:27:09,461
What if its major malfunction
is just benevolence?

330
00:27:11,338 --> 00:27:13,715
What is this? What's he doing?

331
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:17,510
But still, would you prefer
to talk to a real person?

332
00:27:17,636 --> 00:27:20,430
Of course,
but what if that person

333
00:27:20,555 --> 00:27:22,349
is no longer in your life?

334
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:24,517
No longer here?

335
00:27:34,361 --> 00:27:35,570
I've got the file.

336
00:27:36,946 --> 00:27:37,947
Congratulations.

337
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:40,950
Now get out of there
while you still can.

338
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:53,755
Programs, we fight.

339
00:28:15,652 --> 00:28:16,861
Yes!

340
00:28:17,612 --> 00:28:18,947
Thank you so much.

341
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:21,157
What do Paranoiacs do?

342
00:28:21,282 --> 00:28:23,368
Grind you into dust!

343
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:40,051
Caius.

344
00:28:44,848 --> 00:28:47,600
He's dysfunctional. Leave him.

345
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:00,113
You're gonna make it, Caius.

346
00:29:01,698 --> 00:29:03,283
Sometimes you have to
sacrifice your knight

347
00:29:03,408 --> 00:29:05,285
to expose their queen.

348
00:29:30,894 --> 00:29:33,855
...to debut the latest version

349
00:29:33,980 --> 00:29:37,317
of Space Paranoids: Panic City
with the world.

350
00:29:37,442 --> 00:29:38,526
-What's up, bro?
-What is that?

351
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:39,736
-This is crazy.
-Have you seen this?

352
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:42,739
Mr. Singh,
you need to come with me.

353
00:29:42,864 --> 00:29:44,282
This is
a technical difficulty.

354
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:45,492
-We'll be back.
-This way, sir.

355
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:46,868
Everything's gone down.

356
00:29:46,993 --> 00:29:48,620
Well done, Master Control.

357
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:51,790
Eve Kim's file acquired.

358
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:54,501
Objective achieved.

359
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:02,258
Sir, I'm curious
why the Program Caius

360
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:04,302
was not reconstituted.

361
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:09,516
I'm curious
why you are curious.

362
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:14,020
Caius was dysfunctional,
so he was deleted.

363
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:19,901
Just like any program

364
00:30:20,026 --> 00:30:23,404
that operates outside
their directive can be.

365
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:25,490
Do you understand?

366
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:34,123
Acknowledge, Master Control.

367
00:30:34,958 --> 00:30:35,959
Of course.

368
00:30:37,460 --> 00:30:40,672
We are 100% expendable.

369
00:30:41,422 --> 00:30:45,009
New mission, Master Control.
Locate Eve Kim.

370
00:30:46,094 --> 00:30:47,095
Yes, sir.

371
00:30:48,179 --> 00:30:50,515
Seems like we had
a little cyber breach, Jules.

372
00:30:51,224 --> 00:30:52,600
But then of course
you knew that.

373
00:30:52,725 --> 00:30:54,352
It looks like
the whole world knows, buddy.

374
00:30:54,477 --> 00:30:55,854
Might wanna stay off
the socials for a few days.

375
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,897
You wanna play games with me?
Let's play games, Julian.

376
00:30:58,022 --> 00:31:00,483
I heard about your cute
little pitch to the board.

377
00:31:00,608 --> 00:31:03,027
But you left off one
key detail from your deck.

378
00:31:03,152 --> 00:31:04,988
Did you tell them
the shot clock expires

379
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:06,155
at 29 minutes?

380
00:31:06,823 --> 00:31:08,408
Don't make me call The Journal
and tell them

381
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:10,034
you're making promises
you can't keep.

382
00:31:10,159 --> 00:31:11,244
Promises?

383
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:13,079
What, you mean like the one
that your CEO

384
00:31:13,204 --> 00:31:14,372
will be in office
running the company?

385
00:31:14,497 --> 00:31:16,249
Something in the water
over there, Ajay?

386
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,751
I mean, first, wonder boy
Sam Flynn, now his successor.

387
00:31:18,877 --> 00:31:21,671
Where is she, Ajay?
Do you even know where she is?

388
00:31:21,796 --> 00:31:23,006
Maybe you're right.

389
00:31:23,131 --> 00:31:24,507
Maybe Eve went nuts.

390
00:31:24,632 --> 00:31:26,926
Maybe she went AWOL
and left the country,

391
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:28,428
or maybe...

392
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:29,888
she's holed up off the grid

393
00:31:30,013 --> 00:31:31,514
looking for the same
thing you are.

394
00:31:32,098 --> 00:31:33,725
And I know who my money's on.

395
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:35,602
You mean what's left of it
after tonight.

396
00:31:35,727 --> 00:31:36,936
End of line!

397
00:31:38,396 --> 00:31:40,356
I hate that man.

398
00:31:45,028 --> 00:31:45,987
Thank you so much.

399
00:31:46,112 --> 00:31:47,655
You know,
I made those oranges.

400
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,115
It's a long story.

401
00:31:51,034 --> 00:31:53,036
Stop, stop, stop.

402
00:31:54,412 --> 00:31:55,747
What are you doing?

403
00:31:55,872 --> 00:31:58,499
-1913 messages. Popular.
-Wow.

404
00:31:59,709 --> 00:32:01,169
Oh, it's Ajay.
Yeah, that's you.

405
00:32:02,754 --> 00:32:04,547
-Ajay, are you there?
-Am I here?

406
00:32:05,673 --> 00:32:07,550
A brute force attack
took down our servers

407
00:32:07,675 --> 00:32:09,093
during our biggest
product launch in years.

408
00:32:09,218 --> 00:32:11,012
Everything we've built
is melting down.

409
00:32:11,137 --> 00:32:12,388
You need to get back here
right now.

410
00:32:12,513 --> 00:32:14,933
I found it, Ajay. It's real.

411
00:32:15,558 --> 00:32:16,935
Right where
Tess thought it would be.

412
00:32:17,060 --> 00:32:18,811
Flynn had it all along.

413
00:32:18,937 --> 00:32:20,146
Are you talking
about the Permanence Code?

414
00:32:20,271 --> 00:32:22,482
Yeah. Four hours and counting.

415
00:32:22,607 --> 00:32:24,734
Zero degradation,
no instability.

416
00:32:24,859 --> 00:32:25,860
It's incredible.

417
00:32:25,985 --> 00:32:28,029
Wait a second.
Did you say four hours?

418
00:32:28,154 --> 00:32:30,823
-Yeah, four hours.
-My God.

419
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:33,993
He must know, Evie.

420
00:32:34,118 --> 00:32:36,287
-I just spoke to Dillinger.
-Wait.

421
00:32:36,412 --> 00:32:38,247
-You just spoke to Dillinger?
-He's looking

422
00:32:38,373 --> 00:32:39,874
for the code,
and he thinks you are too.

423
00:32:39,999 --> 00:32:41,501
We gotta move on this.

424
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:43,169
Eve,
you've done a great thing.

425
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:45,463
Tess did a great thing.

426
00:32:45,588 --> 00:32:46,798
I'm en route to Encom.

427
00:32:47,006 --> 00:32:49,300
We'll secure the code,
I have it with me on a drive.

428
00:32:54,847 --> 00:32:57,100
We're relaunching Paranoia!

429
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:58,851
Boy, it's your birthday.
Boy, it's your birthday.

430
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,270
-Yeah! Ajay.
-Boy, it's your birthday.

431
00:33:05,775 --> 00:33:07,235
Yo, what's up, Eve?

432
00:33:07,360 --> 00:33:09,320
You've got some news
for the freaks at home?

433
00:33:10,488 --> 00:33:11,531
Um, hi.

434
00:33:12,448 --> 00:33:15,326
"I am fearless,
and therefore powerful."

435
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:18,788
So, apparently we just sold
our ten millionth unit!

436
00:33:20,456 --> 00:33:23,084
Evie , Space Paranoids.

437
00:33:23,209 --> 00:33:26,587
Kevin Flynn,
wherever the hell he is,

438
00:33:26,713 --> 00:33:28,756
has a big smile on his face.

439
00:33:28,881 --> 00:33:30,133
Oh, you crushed it.

440
00:33:32,844 --> 00:33:35,263
No.

441
00:33:39,392 --> 00:33:44,772
♪ Happy birthday to you
Happy birthday to you ♪

442
00:33:48,693 --> 00:33:51,195
♪ Happy birthday, dear Tess ♪

443
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:54,449
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

444
00:34:01,664 --> 00:34:02,749
Breaking news.

445
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:04,667
Encom's Head
of Special Projects,

446
00:34:04,792 --> 00:34:05,918
Tess Kim, died today

447
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,920
after a long battle
with cancer.

448
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:10,673
Her sister, Eve Kim, could not
be reached for comment.

449
00:35:01,015 --> 00:35:02,350
Permanence.

450
00:35:09,941 --> 00:35:10,942
Checkmate.

451
00:35:22,161 --> 00:35:24,997
And so our heroes
venture off into the night.

452
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:26,541
Nothing but
the clothes on their backs

453
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:27,917
and, well,
a six-million-dollar

454
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:29,710
particle laser
that creates organic material

455
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:31,921
out of nowhere,
which is kind of crazy, right?

456
00:35:32,046 --> 00:35:35,925
Keep the equipment safe
and just... lay low.

457
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:37,260
-Okay?
-Yeah.

458
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:39,262
Hey.

459
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:40,805
We got this.

460
00:35:52,775 --> 00:35:53,693
Launch directive

461
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:54,777
on countdown one. Comm check.

462
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:57,155
GNC
on countdown one. Comm check.

463
00:35:57,947 --> 00:35:59,448
Printing in progress.

464
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:01,868
Stage one.
Chamber pressure is nominal.

465
00:36:03,202 --> 00:36:05,121
Envac engine chill has begun.

466
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:15,840
Stage one load is complete.

467
00:36:18,634 --> 00:36:20,011
Transfer complete.

468
00:36:41,824 --> 00:36:43,993
You have 29 minutes
to bring me Eve Kim.

469
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:35,461
Asset deployment confirmed.

470
00:37:35,586 --> 00:37:36,963
Vehicles en route.

471
00:37:43,844 --> 00:37:44,971
Target identified.

472
00:37:45,096 --> 00:37:46,681
Goddamn it. I'm awesome!

473
00:37:46,806 --> 00:37:48,349
Intercepting now.

474
00:38:14,041 --> 00:38:15,042
Eyes on the target.

475
00:38:17,253 --> 00:38:18,587
Coordinating containment

476
00:38:18,713 --> 00:38:20,589
for suspect fleeing eastbound.

477
00:38:25,720 --> 00:38:26,887
What?

478
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:37,940
You, on the motorcycle!

479
00:38:38,065 --> 00:38:38,858
Pull over.

480
00:40:05,069 --> 00:40:06,070
Come on.

481
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:00,249
Where'd she go?

482
00:41:17,308 --> 00:41:18,309
Come on!

483
00:41:20,394 --> 00:41:21,395
Okay.

484
00:41:22,771 --> 00:41:24,398
Come on. Come on. Come on.

485
00:41:40,080 --> 00:41:41,832
Oh, my God.

486
00:41:41,957 --> 00:41:42,958
Come on. Come on.

487
00:42:04,104 --> 00:42:05,064
What?

488
00:42:11,278 --> 00:42:12,154
Okay.

489
00:42:14,156 --> 00:42:18,244
Oh, my God. Okay.

490
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:35,386
Oh, my God!

491
00:43:09,378 --> 00:43:10,754
Prepare the particle laser.

492
00:43:11,338 --> 00:43:12,965
Time to move to plan B.

493
00:43:13,090 --> 00:43:14,341
Yes, sir.

494
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:31,900
Come on.

495
00:43:37,531 --> 00:43:38,991
Come on.

496
00:43:39,658 --> 00:43:40,618
Yeah.

497
00:44:32,127 --> 00:44:33,671
Oh, yeah. You wanna play?

498
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,269
What are you?

499
00:46:12,978 --> 00:46:15,272
I am Master Control.

500
00:46:26,366 --> 00:46:27,367
What do you want?

501
00:46:27,493 --> 00:46:28,952
I want the code.

502
00:46:29,495 --> 00:46:30,496
Well...

503
00:46:31,205 --> 00:46:32,206
It's gone.

504
00:46:37,836 --> 00:46:40,047
No, it's not.

505
00:46:45,177 --> 00:46:46,178
I have her in my sights.

506
00:46:46,345 --> 00:46:48,055
Establishing connection
to the Grid now.

507
00:46:48,180 --> 00:46:51,517
Ready to transfer
in T-minus 15 seconds.

508
00:46:51,642 --> 00:46:54,895
You're... a program.

509
00:47:05,531 --> 00:47:07,574
You're timing out.

510
00:47:12,412 --> 00:47:13,872
Get on the ground!

511
00:47:23,298 --> 00:47:24,591
Transfer her into the Grid.

512
00:47:33,433 --> 00:47:34,977
I'm on
the ground in downtown.

513
00:47:35,102 --> 00:47:37,855
And I can tell you,
this was no elaborate stunt.

514
00:47:37,980 --> 00:47:40,607
-Three riders...
-What have you done?

515
00:47:41,692 --> 00:47:44,194
How could you be so reckless?

516
00:47:44,319 --> 00:47:47,239
When the world sees
what I have created,

517
00:47:47,364 --> 00:47:49,157
all will be forgiven.

518
00:47:50,242 --> 00:47:52,119
Is that what you think?

519
00:47:52,911 --> 00:47:57,457
You think that
you're in control of this?

520
00:47:58,417 --> 00:47:59,835
You're not.

521
00:47:59,960 --> 00:48:01,670
Believing we can
change the world

522
00:48:01,795 --> 00:48:03,755
is what keeps
this company relevant.

523
00:48:03,881 --> 00:48:07,426
But it's also what can burn it
to the ground.

524
00:48:08,343 --> 00:48:13,515
And your job
is knowing the difference.

525
00:48:17,102 --> 00:48:19,313
Transfer
of biological life-form

526
00:48:19,438 --> 00:48:20,606
in progress.

527
00:48:22,357 --> 00:48:24,443
Digital reconstruction
initiated.

528
00:48:26,111 --> 00:48:28,363
Twenty percent digitized.

529
00:48:29,865 --> 00:48:31,700
Forty percent digitized.

530
00:48:33,785 --> 00:48:35,829
Sixty-five percent digitized.

531
00:48:38,123 --> 00:48:40,042
Ninety-five percent digitized.

532
00:48:43,253 --> 00:48:44,796
Digitization complete.

533
00:48:45,464 --> 00:48:48,550
Run diagnostics
and scan for corruption.

534
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:08,737
Eve Kim
identity disk activated.

535
00:49:31,426 --> 00:49:32,678
Wow.

536
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:37,641
Where am I?

537
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:41,728
Dillinger Systems
Central Processing Unit.

538
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:44,064
Wait. What?

539
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:49,277
We have identified
the sequence.

540
00:49:50,404 --> 00:49:52,114
The user possesses the code.

541
00:49:52,239 --> 00:49:53,198
The code?

542
00:49:54,324 --> 00:49:55,534
The code?

543
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:57,661
I don't have the code.
I destroyed the drive.

544
00:49:57,786 --> 00:49:59,579
Silence, user.

545
00:49:59,705 --> 00:50:01,790
The code isn't only
on a drive.

546
00:50:01,915 --> 00:50:02,916
The code is inside of you.

547
00:50:03,041 --> 00:50:04,418
Whether you remember it
or not,

548
00:50:04,543 --> 00:50:06,628
you've seen it
and that is enough.

549
00:50:06,753 --> 00:50:08,296
Sir, her disk is showing
signs of instability.

550
00:50:08,422 --> 00:50:09,881
Define instability.

551
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:12,426
Extraction of the code
may result in de-resolution

552
00:50:12,551 --> 00:50:13,510
of the carrier.

553
00:50:13,635 --> 00:50:14,928
The directive is clear.

554
00:50:15,053 --> 00:50:18,807
Isolate the thread
and commence extraction.

555
00:50:18,932 --> 00:50:20,851
Copy.

556
00:50:20,976 --> 00:50:23,437
Wait. No, no, no.

557
00:50:23,562 --> 00:50:24,521
Stop.

558
00:50:25,772 --> 00:50:27,524
Athena is correct.

559
00:50:28,316 --> 00:50:30,986
There's only one user
whose directive we follow.

560
00:50:47,502 --> 00:50:48,879
What will remain of the user

561
00:50:49,004 --> 00:50:51,006
if she were to suffer
de-resolution?

562
00:50:51,882 --> 00:50:53,008
Nothing, sir.

563
00:50:53,133 --> 00:50:55,260
No trace of her existence
on the Grid?

564
00:50:55,385 --> 00:50:57,387
None, sir.

565
00:51:09,566 --> 00:51:12,110
Extract the code
and delete the carrier.

566
00:51:13,653 --> 00:51:16,448
But, sir, extracting
the Permanence Code

567
00:51:16,573 --> 00:51:19,868
would delete the carrier from
the Grid and from your world.

568
00:51:29,127 --> 00:51:30,378
Once upon a time,

569
00:51:30,504 --> 00:51:32,839
there was a weapon
and its name was Ares.

570
00:51:32,964 --> 00:51:35,717
And Ares obeyed every command
of Julian Dillinger,

571
00:51:35,842 --> 00:51:38,386
and Julian Dillinger
made a trillion dollars.

572
00:51:38,512 --> 00:51:42,432
And wrote his name
on the face of time in blood.

573
00:51:42,974 --> 00:51:45,769
Now, whatever PEBKAC error
is behind these feelings,

574
00:51:45,894 --> 00:51:49,064
I'm going to find it
and rip it out of you.

575
00:51:49,189 --> 00:51:51,191
Do I make myself clear?

576
00:51:52,943 --> 00:51:54,361
Perfectly.

577
00:51:54,486 --> 00:51:56,488
Program dismissed.

578
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:03,870
The creature also said,
"I am fearless,

579
00:52:05,789 --> 00:52:07,374
and therefore powerful."

580
00:52:19,219 --> 00:52:20,262
Well?

581
00:52:20,387 --> 00:52:21,638
The user is indisposed.

582
00:52:21,763 --> 00:52:23,348
Hold extraction
until further directive.

583
00:52:23,473 --> 00:52:24,766
-Indisposed?
-Correct.

584
00:52:24,891 --> 00:52:26,726
Define indisposed.

585
00:52:29,396 --> 00:52:31,398
He's stuck in traffic.

586
00:52:32,566 --> 00:52:35,026
No, he's at the opera.

587
00:52:35,777 --> 00:52:37,696
He's standing on
the top of Mount Fuji

588
00:52:37,821 --> 00:52:38,864
in a pair of green socks

589
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:40,949
playing "Pistol Packin' Mama"
on the mandolin.

590
00:52:41,074 --> 00:52:42,826
I gave you an order.

591
00:52:42,951 --> 00:52:44,703
The creator is indisposed.

592
00:52:44,828 --> 00:52:48,165
Hold extraction until
we receive further directive.

593
00:52:48,290 --> 00:52:50,167
Do I make myself clear?

594
00:52:52,127 --> 00:52:53,128
Yes, sir.

595
00:52:53,795 --> 00:52:55,380
Programs dismissed.

596
00:53:08,810 --> 00:53:09,853
Can I trust you?

597
00:53:10,228 --> 00:53:12,814
It's a complicated question.
How much time you got?

598
00:53:12,939 --> 00:53:14,024
Sixty seconds. Answer now.

599
00:53:14,149 --> 00:53:15,483
Your life cycle
depends upon it.

600
00:53:15,609 --> 00:53:17,444
I don't have a life cycle.

601
00:53:17,569 --> 00:53:20,238
Yes, you do.
For another 54 seconds.

602
00:53:20,363 --> 00:53:21,823
Can I trust you?

603
00:53:21,948 --> 00:53:25,744
Um, I'd like to think so,
but probably not.

604
00:53:34,044 --> 00:53:37,255
Where is Master Control?

605
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:39,049
Sir, Master Control
is exhibiting

606
00:53:39,174 --> 00:53:40,508
signs of malfunction.

607
00:53:41,509 --> 00:53:42,761
Hmm.

608
00:53:48,850 --> 00:53:51,645
Any threat to the directive
must be eliminated.

609
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:55,148
Extract the code
and delete them both.

610
00:53:55,273 --> 00:53:57,317
-Do you understand?
-Hmm.

611
00:54:00,445 --> 00:54:02,864
-And Julian Dillinger?
-You can't trust him.

612
00:54:02,989 --> 00:54:06,993
For him, everyone
and everything is expendable.

613
00:54:10,205 --> 00:54:11,289
I miscalculated.

614
00:54:11,414 --> 00:54:12,707
We have a new directive.

615
00:54:15,210 --> 00:54:16,962
Athena, it doesn't have to
be like this.

616
00:54:20,757 --> 00:54:22,133
Delete him!

617
00:56:11,034 --> 00:56:13,286
I'm okay. I'm okay.

618
00:56:15,872 --> 00:56:17,957
They're headed
towards the Transfer Portal.

619
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:20,168
We lost them in the Grid,
ma'am.

620
00:56:22,295 --> 00:56:23,505
Preparing the drones.

621
00:56:32,430 --> 00:56:34,891
Delete Ares, and bring
the user back to me.

622
00:56:35,016 --> 00:56:35,975
Copy.

623
00:56:55,203 --> 00:56:56,955
What happened back there?

624
00:56:57,080 --> 00:56:59,165
I disobeyed my directive.

625
00:56:59,290 --> 00:57:00,250
Which was?

626
00:57:00,375 --> 00:57:02,293
To retrieve the code
from your disk

627
00:57:02,419 --> 00:57:03,795
and delete the carrier.

628
00:57:05,630 --> 00:57:07,674
Dillinger told you
to delete me?

629
00:57:13,430 --> 00:57:14,431
Hang on!

630
00:57:16,975 --> 00:57:18,560
Where are they?

631
00:57:18,685 --> 00:57:20,562
Scanning
quadrants three and four.

632
00:57:20,687 --> 00:57:21,771
Sector 18 clear.

633
00:57:25,400 --> 00:57:26,526
Where are we going?

634
00:57:26,651 --> 00:57:28,111
Transfer Portal.

635
00:57:28,236 --> 00:57:29,612
It's the only way
out of the Grid.

636
00:57:29,737 --> 00:57:31,990
You'll be reconstituted
in the real world

637
00:57:32,115 --> 00:57:34,534
exactly as you were before,
hypothetically.

638
00:57:37,620 --> 00:57:39,164
-Hypothetically?
-Probably.

639
00:57:39,914 --> 00:57:41,875
We have movement in sector 72.

640
00:57:42,667 --> 00:57:44,127
Zeroing in on target.

641
00:57:44,878 --> 00:57:46,296
Shut them down!

642
00:57:56,347 --> 00:57:58,766
You wanna get home,
I can help you.

643
00:57:58,892 --> 00:58:01,186
But I need something
in return.

644
00:58:01,311 --> 00:58:02,979
I told you
I don't have the code.

645
00:58:04,439 --> 00:58:07,317
You found it once,
you can find it again.

646
00:58:07,442 --> 00:58:08,693
So you can give it
to Dillinger?

647
00:58:12,405 --> 00:58:13,490
Not for Dillinger.

648
00:58:14,032 --> 00:58:15,033
For me.

649
00:58:18,119 --> 00:58:19,787
Do we have a deal?

650
00:58:56,074 --> 00:58:57,450
So, do we have a deal?

651
00:58:57,575 --> 00:58:59,536
Yes. Yes, I know
where to find the code.

652
00:58:59,661 --> 00:59:00,745
Just get me out of here.

653
00:59:09,170 --> 00:59:11,214
Target
approaching Transfer Portal

654
00:59:11,339 --> 00:59:12,423
in 45 seconds.

655
00:59:42,787 --> 00:59:44,872
Drones
malfunctioned and offline.

656
01:00:14,652 --> 01:00:17,864
Attention.
Please stand clear.

657
01:00:20,867 --> 01:00:22,076
Override not responding.

658
01:00:22,201 --> 01:00:22,994
Transfer bay is online.

659
01:00:23,661 --> 01:00:24,829
-What is it?
-Who authorized this?

660
01:00:25,455 --> 01:00:27,915
Sir, this originated
inside the Grid.

661
01:00:28,041 --> 01:00:28,875
Julian?

662
01:00:29,626 --> 01:00:30,627
All agents
report to transfer bay floor

663
01:00:30,752 --> 01:00:31,544
immediately.

664
01:00:31,669 --> 01:00:33,087
Clear the area.

665
01:00:33,212 --> 01:00:34,005
Get everybody out of here.

666
01:00:34,547 --> 01:00:36,466
Unauthorized printing
in progress.

667
01:00:36,591 --> 01:00:38,968
Clear the central area.

668
01:00:43,931 --> 01:00:45,099
Transfer complete.

669
01:00:45,224 --> 01:00:46,184
Move in.

670
01:01:07,205 --> 01:01:08,665
Well, well, well.

671
01:01:08,790 --> 01:01:10,750
Just got double-crossed
by my program.

672
01:01:11,459 --> 01:01:13,961
It wants the Permanence Code
for itself.

673
01:01:15,755 --> 01:01:17,048
Eve, is that the deal?

674
01:01:17,173 --> 01:01:18,257
It gets you out of the Grid,

675
01:01:18,383 --> 01:01:19,926
you turn Pinocchio
into a real boy?

676
01:01:20,051 --> 01:01:21,135
Well, you're missing the part

677
01:01:21,260 --> 01:01:22,512
where you're willing
to commit murder

678
01:01:22,637 --> 01:01:23,763
for a piece of software.

679
01:01:23,888 --> 01:01:24,847
Is that what it said?

680
01:01:24,972 --> 01:01:26,349
Twenty-eight minutes,
41 seconds.

681
01:01:26,849 --> 01:01:28,476
Ares!

682
01:01:28,601 --> 01:01:30,311
I do hope
this works out for you.

683
01:01:30,436 --> 01:01:32,563
There's no second chances,
no do-overs.

684
01:01:32,689 --> 01:01:35,775
These are the last 29 minutes
you'll ever have!

685
01:01:35,900 --> 01:01:37,527
Better make it count!

686
01:02:04,637 --> 01:02:06,305
I should've majored
in English lit.

687
01:02:23,823 --> 01:02:25,616
Transfer complete.

688
01:02:28,035 --> 01:02:29,412
Your directive is
to find Eve Kim,

689
01:02:29,537 --> 01:02:32,206
return her to the Grid and
get me the Permanence Code.

690
01:02:32,331 --> 01:02:34,000
By any means necessary.

691
01:02:34,584 --> 01:02:36,961
Do you understand
your directive,

692
01:02:37,086 --> 01:02:39,464
Master Control?

693
01:02:46,554 --> 01:02:47,889
At your command, sir.

694
01:02:48,556 --> 01:02:49,557
Attagirl.

695
01:03:09,619 --> 01:03:10,995
Ticktock!

696
01:03:12,663 --> 01:03:13,873
Oh!

697
01:03:14,540 --> 01:03:16,876
Oh!

698
01:03:17,001 --> 01:03:18,628
Whoo!

699
01:03:21,297 --> 01:03:25,468
Now that is the coolest thing
I have ever seen.

700
01:03:40,274 --> 01:03:41,526
Do you know
who Kevin Flynn was?

701
01:03:41,651 --> 01:03:44,153
Of course.
Visionary programmer,

702
01:03:44,278 --> 01:03:45,696
pioneer of
The Digital Frontier .

703
01:03:45,822 --> 01:03:47,490
Disappeared 1989.

704
01:03:47,615 --> 01:03:50,076
I found the Permanence Code
on a backup of Flynn's server.

705
01:03:50,201 --> 01:03:53,120
That server is at Encom's
office downtown.

706
01:03:53,246 --> 01:03:54,413
But we can make it within...

707
01:03:54,539 --> 01:03:55,957
Twenty-six minutes,
nine seconds.

708
01:03:57,458 --> 01:04:00,086
Eve, your plan contains
two major flaws.

709
01:04:00,211 --> 01:04:01,212
Okay.

710
01:04:01,337 --> 01:04:03,840
One, Encom is 9.2 miles away,

711
01:04:03,965 --> 01:04:04,924
given our present speed

712
01:04:05,049 --> 01:04:06,843
and suboptimal
choice of vehicle...

713
01:04:06,968 --> 01:04:07,885
Oh, my God.

714
01:04:08,177 --> 01:04:09,470
Two, we're gonna need
a particle laser.

715
01:04:11,639 --> 01:04:12,723
We need a phone.

716
01:04:28,030 --> 01:04:29,740
I cannot believe
I'm doing this.

717
01:04:31,617 --> 01:04:34,662
Excuse me. Do you see this?
This is me.

718
01:04:34,787 --> 01:04:36,080
If you let me use
your cell phone,

719
01:04:36,205 --> 01:04:38,916
my assistant
will wire you $10,000.

720
01:04:39,041 --> 01:04:40,251
I just need your phone.

721
01:04:48,009 --> 01:04:49,510
Seth, where are you?

722
01:04:49,635 --> 01:04:51,345
Eve,
whose phone is this?

723
01:04:51,470 --> 01:04:54,265
Listen to me. I need you
at Encom in 15 minutes.

724
01:04:54,390 --> 01:04:55,600
Hey, is everything okay?

725
01:04:55,725 --> 01:04:58,519
Seth, bring
the particle laser.

726
01:04:58,644 --> 01:05:00,396
Encom, 15 minutes. Got it.

727
01:05:01,856 --> 01:05:03,107
That's my car.

728
01:05:03,232 --> 01:05:04,317
I'll wire you another 50K.

729
01:05:04,442 --> 01:05:05,651
Hey, that's my car!

730
01:05:05,776 --> 01:05:07,945
The Honda Civic 2.0
four-cylinder

731
01:05:08,070 --> 01:05:09,989
with 138 horsepower.

732
01:05:10,573 --> 01:05:11,574
Classic.

733
01:05:11,699 --> 01:05:13,159
Hey! That's my car!

734
01:05:13,951 --> 01:05:15,953
That's my car!

735
01:05:37,642 --> 01:05:39,310
God.

736
01:05:41,270 --> 01:05:42,688
-Eve?
-Yeah?

737
01:05:42,813 --> 01:05:44,857
I was thinking about the time
you told your sister

738
01:05:44,982 --> 01:05:47,860
that you wished you never
relaunched Space Paranoids .

739
01:05:47,985 --> 01:05:49,195
Then you went on
to say that...

740
01:05:49,320 --> 01:05:51,405
Oh, my God. Of course.
You read all my texts.

741
01:05:51,530 --> 01:05:54,659
Yeah. Yeah, I've read
them all. Every single one.

742
01:05:54,784 --> 01:05:55,743
Wow.

743
01:05:56,160 --> 01:05:57,787
Most of it was information
of a personal nature.

744
01:05:57,912 --> 01:06:00,164
Some of it, highly personal.

745
01:06:00,289 --> 01:06:02,959
And I just can't get enough.

746
01:06:03,751 --> 01:06:04,877
What?

747
01:06:05,670 --> 01:06:09,757
Depeche Mode. Number eight
on the UK singles chart, 1982.

748
01:06:09,882 --> 01:06:11,550
I find their brand of
pithy, catchy,

749
01:06:11,676 --> 01:06:13,386
timeless and true
'80s electropop

750
01:06:13,511 --> 01:06:16,347
to be deeply invigorating.

751
01:06:25,022 --> 01:06:27,358
Sixteen minutes, 20 seconds.

752
01:06:27,483 --> 01:06:29,860
Okay. So you like,
uh, '80s pop

753
01:06:29,986 --> 01:06:32,363
and, uh, cyber-spying on me.

754
01:06:32,488 --> 01:06:34,073
I was directed
to kill you, Eve.

755
01:06:34,198 --> 01:06:36,534
Hacking seems pretty tame
by comparison.

756
01:06:40,246 --> 01:06:41,664
-Oh, my God.
-For the record,

757
01:06:41,789 --> 01:06:44,000
I don't think you have
anything to be ashamed of.

758
01:06:44,125 --> 01:06:45,501
Space Paranoids
has entertained

759
01:06:45,626 --> 01:06:46,794
hundreds of millions.

760
01:06:46,919 --> 01:06:48,504
Plus, it's a pretty cool game.

761
01:06:49,296 --> 01:06:51,382
Anyway, you told your sister
that designing games

762
01:06:51,507 --> 01:06:53,384
left you feeling
hollow, broken.

763
01:06:53,509 --> 01:06:54,552
Was it that your work
was about

764
01:06:54,677 --> 01:06:55,803
entertainment and profits

765
01:06:56,137 --> 01:06:58,389
and her work was about
improving the human condition?

766
01:06:58,514 --> 01:07:00,474
Your texts suggest
a certain fixation

767
01:07:00,599 --> 01:07:02,560
with not being able to live up
to her standards,

768
01:07:02,685 --> 01:07:04,270
which must have
been complicated,

769
01:07:04,395 --> 01:07:06,647
especially considering
she was the younger sister.

770
01:07:06,772 --> 01:07:08,566
Okay. Watch it.

771
01:07:09,150 --> 01:07:10,735
By the way, I don't think
you should quit.

772
01:07:13,863 --> 01:07:15,114
What do you mean?

773
01:07:15,239 --> 01:07:17,366
Your plan upon returning
from the mountains,

774
01:07:17,491 --> 01:07:18,451
if I read you correctly,

775
01:07:18,743 --> 01:07:20,161
was to hand over
the Permanence Code to Encom

776
01:07:20,286 --> 01:07:22,955
and then let them figure out
what to do with it next, no?

777
01:07:26,917 --> 01:07:28,586
Yeah. Now I understand.

778
01:07:28,711 --> 01:07:30,296
You completed her work

779
01:07:30,421 --> 01:07:32,131
as a way to
stay connected to her.

780
01:07:33,883 --> 01:07:35,009
Huh.

781
01:07:35,134 --> 01:07:36,510
And now what?

782
01:07:38,637 --> 01:07:40,890
Being human is hard.

783
01:07:41,557 --> 01:07:43,768
The things that make life
great are the same things

784
01:07:43,893 --> 01:07:49,106
that make it excruciating,
like love, loss.

785
01:07:56,280 --> 01:07:57,948
You must miss her very much.

786
01:08:10,044 --> 01:08:11,337
Hey, hey.

787
01:08:11,462 --> 01:08:12,421
What the hell?

788
01:08:13,589 --> 01:08:14,757
Whoa.
Check this guy out.

789
01:08:16,550 --> 01:08:18,260
-Well, look who it is!
-Hi.

790
01:08:18,385 --> 01:08:19,428
Glad you could join us,
Miss Kim.

791
01:08:19,678 --> 01:08:20,679
People have been wondering
where you've been.

792
01:08:21,097 --> 01:08:22,556
Long time no see. Bit of
a rush, so I'm just gonna...

793
01:08:22,681 --> 01:08:23,474
-Eve.
-Mm-hmm?

794
01:08:23,599 --> 01:08:24,600
You gotta bring your badge.

795
01:08:25,184 --> 01:08:27,019
Okay, yeah, Jolene...

796
01:08:27,144 --> 01:08:30,064
Hello, Jolene. Hi.
Got her badge right here.

797
01:08:30,189 --> 01:08:31,273
Okay. His too?

798
01:08:31,398 --> 01:08:33,109
Uh, no. He's not with us.

799
01:08:33,234 --> 01:08:34,485
-Yes, he is.
-Yes, he is.

800
01:08:39,198 --> 01:08:41,492
Let's start literally
anywhere you'd like. Um...

801
01:08:43,035 --> 01:08:44,537
This is my boyfriend, Ares.

802
01:08:45,830 --> 01:08:48,707
No. Master Control
Security Program

803
01:08:48,833 --> 01:08:49,875
from Dillinger's Grid.

804
01:08:50,000 --> 01:08:52,044
Ares, Seth. Seth, Ares.
Oh, God.

805
01:08:52,169 --> 01:08:53,129
Pleasure.

806
01:08:53,254 --> 01:08:54,213
Hey, that's nice.

807
01:08:54,630 --> 01:08:57,299
Um, so, Ares, like, as in,
the god of war, Ares?

808
01:08:59,009 --> 01:09:00,010
Yeah.

809
01:09:00,136 --> 01:09:02,346
Cool. You're Greek.
That's awesome.

810
01:09:02,471 --> 01:09:03,430
So when you say that

811
01:09:03,848 --> 01:09:04,849
he's the security program,
do you mean he's like...

812
01:09:04,974 --> 01:09:06,350
-Yeah. He's not human.
-He's not human.

813
01:09:06,475 --> 01:09:07,935
-Mm-hmm.
-Originated inside a GPU.

814
01:09:09,145 --> 01:09:11,147
Okay. Is this
for the Christmas video?

815
01:09:13,357 --> 01:09:15,192
Three minutes
to de-resolution.

816
01:09:15,317 --> 01:09:16,443
Can you work with that, Seth?

817
01:09:16,569 --> 01:09:17,528
Yeah.

818
01:09:18,696 --> 01:09:20,030
Don't need help, guys.

819
01:09:20,156 --> 01:09:21,115
Okay.

820
01:09:22,241 --> 01:09:23,242
Oh, boy.

821
01:09:29,748 --> 01:09:32,293
So, this is where
I found the Permanence Code

822
01:09:32,418 --> 01:09:33,961
on a backup of this server.

823
01:09:40,009 --> 01:09:41,802
Talk about first gen.

824
01:09:41,927 --> 01:09:44,221
Talk about a piece of garbage.
Am I right?

825
01:09:44,346 --> 01:09:46,015
That was super insensitive
to your ancestors,

826
01:09:46,140 --> 01:09:46,932
and I'm so sorry.

827
01:09:47,516 --> 01:09:49,435
It's gonna take me
a few minutes to set this up.

828
01:09:49,560 --> 01:09:51,687
No rush. Two minutes,
18 seconds.

829
01:09:52,855 --> 01:09:55,024
Soon as the laser's up,
we'll send you into the Grid.

830
01:09:55,149 --> 01:09:56,859
Once you're in there, you'll
have to run your own search,

831
01:09:56,984 --> 01:09:59,195
but believe me, the Permanence
Code is in there.

832
01:09:59,320 --> 01:10:00,487
So what should I expect?

833
01:10:00,613 --> 01:10:04,241
Uh, if I were to guess?
Think '80s.

834
01:10:04,366 --> 01:10:05,201
'80s.

835
01:10:05,784 --> 01:10:07,036
I like the '80s.

836
01:10:07,620 --> 01:10:09,413
One minute, 31 seconds.

837
01:10:10,748 --> 01:10:11,582
Okay. Come on.

838
01:10:12,583 --> 01:10:13,584
Please, help me.

839
01:10:14,418 --> 01:10:15,711
Okay, all set.

840
01:10:15,836 --> 01:10:16,879
Adapters.

841
01:10:18,422 --> 01:10:19,632
Once you locate the code,

842
01:10:19,757 --> 01:10:21,926
get to the portal
and we'll bring you out.

843
01:10:22,760 --> 01:10:24,428
I'll activate it
from the outside.

844
01:10:25,596 --> 01:10:27,014
Can I trust you?

845
01:10:30,643 --> 01:10:31,769
I'd like to think so,

846
01:10:31,894 --> 01:10:33,562
-but probably not.
-Probably not.

847
01:10:34,063 --> 01:10:35,064
Yeah.

848
01:10:35,439 --> 01:10:36,982
Well, it's a good thing
we don't have trust issues

849
01:10:37,107 --> 01:10:38,484
because if we did,
I could imagine that--

850
01:10:38,609 --> 01:10:39,568
I could pull the plug

851
01:10:40,110 --> 01:10:42,655
and leave you in a Grid less
complex than my smartphone

852
01:10:42,780 --> 01:10:44,531
for all eternity.

853
01:10:45,032 --> 01:10:46,325
The thought had
crossed my mind.

854
01:10:46,450 --> 01:10:47,952
Mine too.

855
01:10:48,077 --> 01:10:49,036
Oh, mine three.

856
01:10:49,703 --> 01:10:50,704
Sorry. Just...

857
01:10:53,290 --> 01:10:54,667
Well, here goes nothing.

858
01:10:55,251 --> 01:10:56,710
Or here goes something.

859
01:10:58,337 --> 01:10:59,338
You're right.

860
01:11:00,965 --> 01:11:01,966
I do miss her.

861
01:11:03,759 --> 01:11:05,094
All the time.

862
01:11:09,515 --> 01:11:11,684
Athena. She's here.

863
01:11:15,688 --> 01:11:17,773
Whoa. What is that?

864
01:11:18,274 --> 01:11:19,608
Athena.

865
01:11:19,733 --> 01:11:20,693
Wait. Who?

866
01:11:20,818 --> 01:11:23,070
Seth, the laser. The laser!

867
01:11:23,195 --> 01:11:25,072
Okay, initiating systems now.

868
01:11:25,197 --> 01:11:26,615
Connecting to the Flynn Grid.

869
01:11:32,705 --> 01:11:34,039
Firing up the laser.

870
01:11:35,582 --> 01:11:36,917
Wait, what's she doing?

871
01:11:37,042 --> 01:11:38,585
She's waiting for me
to time out...

872
01:11:39,753 --> 01:11:41,380
...and then she'll come
for you.

873
01:11:45,759 --> 01:11:47,553
We're almost there. Get ready.

874
01:11:47,678 --> 01:11:48,721
Come on.
Hurry, hurry, hurry.

875
01:11:49,305 --> 01:11:51,223
Ares, move
in front of the laser.

876
01:11:53,809 --> 01:11:55,019
Okay. We're ready.

877
01:11:55,936 --> 01:11:57,062
What are you doing?

878
01:11:58,981 --> 01:11:59,982
Come on.

879
01:12:04,611 --> 01:12:06,405
Change of plans.

880
01:12:08,824 --> 01:12:10,743
-No, no, no!
-No, wait!

881
01:12:51,158 --> 01:12:52,493
Well, that actually worked.

882
01:13:01,043 --> 01:13:02,544
-He's inside.
-Great.

883
01:13:10,219 --> 01:13:11,178
Move!

884
01:13:48,257 --> 01:13:49,299
Eve.

885
01:14:09,319 --> 01:14:11,113
Time to get back to the Grid.

886
01:14:11,238 --> 01:14:12,197
Leave her alone!

887
01:14:49,234 --> 01:14:52,196
You're very persistent, user.

888
01:15:55,801 --> 01:15:56,760
What?

889
01:15:59,179 --> 01:16:00,389
Hi.

890
01:16:02,683 --> 01:16:03,934
Did we win?

891
01:16:04,059 --> 01:16:06,353
She'll be back.

892
01:16:07,604 --> 01:16:08,814
Ares.

893
01:16:10,023 --> 01:16:11,441
He can't get out.

894
01:16:36,883 --> 01:16:38,343
The '80s.

895
01:16:50,314 --> 01:16:51,440
Binary digit.

896
01:16:52,065 --> 01:16:54,192
-You're a Bit.
-Yes.

897
01:16:56,111 --> 01:16:58,071
I'm looking for something.
Can you help me find it?

898
01:16:58,196 --> 01:16:59,615
Yes, yes, yes.

899
01:17:14,755 --> 01:17:15,756
Classic.

900
01:17:42,532 --> 01:17:44,785
I'm surrounded by
the wide-scale destruction

901
01:17:44,910 --> 01:17:46,787
caused by tonight's
brazen attack

902
01:17:46,912 --> 01:17:48,872
that left local residents
stunned.

903
01:17:48,997 --> 01:17:50,957
There is speculation that
Dillinger Systems

904
01:17:51,083 --> 01:17:52,793
had something to do
with the event,

905
01:17:52,918 --> 01:17:54,336
and authorities have
remained tight-lipped.

906
01:17:54,461 --> 01:17:55,587
Citizens

907
01:17:55,712 --> 01:17:57,130
and authorities alike
want to know...

908
01:17:57,255 --> 01:18:00,967
was this a coordinated attack
or technology run amok?

909
01:18:01,093 --> 01:18:02,386
What now?

910
01:18:17,859 --> 01:18:19,361
What is this?

911
01:18:20,529 --> 01:18:21,530
Where's my code?

912
01:18:23,073 --> 01:18:24,074
Hey!

913
01:18:25,033 --> 01:18:27,160
What are you doing?
Who gave you this directive?

914
01:18:28,036 --> 01:18:29,329
You did, sir.

915
01:18:34,710 --> 01:18:35,877
What is this?

916
01:18:37,546 --> 01:18:38,880
Warning.

917
01:18:40,257 --> 01:18:41,425
No, no, no.

918
01:18:41,550 --> 01:18:43,135
This is too big, Athena.
Too big!

919
01:18:43,260 --> 01:18:44,469
Julian!

920
01:18:44,594 --> 01:18:45,762
You're done.

921
01:18:46,304 --> 01:18:47,848
The board is moving
as we speak

922
01:18:47,973 --> 01:18:49,099
to strip you of your title,

923
01:18:49,224 --> 01:18:51,351
and I'm reassuming control
of the company.

924
01:18:51,476 --> 01:18:53,603
No, you can't do that.
Can't do that!

925
01:18:53,729 --> 01:18:55,272
Yes, I can.

926
01:18:55,397 --> 01:18:57,149
This is not going any further.

927
01:18:58,525 --> 01:18:59,651
You can't...

928
01:18:59,776 --> 01:19:01,528
My first order of business
is shutting down

929
01:19:01,653 --> 01:19:03,905
-The Permanence Project.
-No, no, no. Mom, no!

930
01:19:08,577 --> 01:19:10,746
Don't be afraid.

931
01:19:12,956 --> 01:19:14,958
We gave a thousand lives
for the Grid.

932
01:19:18,336 --> 01:19:20,464
You only have to give one.

933
01:19:21,882 --> 01:19:23,008
No, no, no.

934
01:19:23,133 --> 01:19:24,718
Mom!

935
01:19:30,515 --> 01:19:32,267
Impediment eliminated.

936
01:19:33,310 --> 01:19:36,021
What did you do?
What did you do?

937
01:19:37,856 --> 01:19:39,357
I am fulfilling my directive.

938
01:19:39,858 --> 01:19:40,859
Capture Eve Kim.

939
01:19:41,109 --> 01:19:43,820
Return her to the Grid
by any means necessary.

940
01:19:44,988 --> 01:19:46,865
Scanning
for further impediments.

941
01:19:52,746 --> 01:19:53,997
Please keep clear.

942
01:20:05,050 --> 01:20:06,510
Hang on, Mom. Hang on.

943
01:20:15,185 --> 01:20:16,603
No!

944
01:21:20,876 --> 01:21:21,877
Flynn.

945
01:21:25,964 --> 01:21:27,591
Greetings, program.

946
01:21:50,780 --> 01:21:52,574
Oh, God. Not good.

947
01:21:52,699 --> 01:21:54,242
There are multiple reports

948
01:21:54,367 --> 01:21:56,244
of fire and destruction
on the upper levels...

949
01:21:56,369 --> 01:21:57,370
Um, Eve?

950
01:21:57,871 --> 01:21:59,372
What the hell happened
to our office?

951
01:21:59,497 --> 01:22:00,832
Ajay, look, there's no time.

952
01:22:00,957 --> 01:22:02,959
The Dillingers transported me
inside their server

953
01:22:03,084 --> 01:22:04,628
by reversing the direction
of a particle laser.

954
01:22:04,753 --> 01:22:07,047
-Not this one. Theirs.
-That's impossible.

955
01:22:07,172 --> 01:22:09,925
No. A scary lady did it, man.
She threw me... It was wild.

956
01:22:10,842 --> 01:22:12,761
I saw a complex world

957
01:22:12,886 --> 01:22:15,055
where packets of energy
move as vehicles

958
01:22:15,180 --> 01:22:17,223
that trail by lines of light.

959
01:22:17,349 --> 01:22:20,101
And-And programs
take on human form.

960
01:22:20,769 --> 01:22:23,897
I met the most advanced AI
known to mankind.

961
01:22:24,564 --> 01:22:25,440
His name is Ares.

962
01:22:26,107 --> 01:22:27,525
Like the god of war, but he's
actually a super nice guy.

963
01:22:27,651 --> 01:22:28,735
-Sorry.
-Right now,

964
01:22:28,860 --> 01:22:31,279
Ares is inside
Flynn's original server.

965
01:22:31,404 --> 01:22:32,864
He's looking
for the Permanence Code.

966
01:22:32,989 --> 01:22:34,324
I have to bring him back here,

967
01:22:34,449 --> 01:22:36,451
and I'm not going to be able
to do that

968
01:22:36,576 --> 01:22:38,286
until we fix this laser.

969
01:22:38,995 --> 01:22:41,915
I don't understand.
Are you alive?

970
01:22:42,040 --> 01:22:45,502
I exist in this moment
because you do.

971
01:22:46,795 --> 01:22:49,464
A reflection of your presence.

972
01:22:50,840 --> 01:22:52,717
What's your story?

973
01:22:52,842 --> 01:22:56,429
I'm Ares, Master Control of
the Dillinger Security Grid.

974
01:22:57,263 --> 01:22:58,264
Dillinger?

975
01:22:58,848 --> 01:23:00,475
Hmm.

976
01:23:00,600 --> 01:23:03,144
Well, we both know
you can't get here from there.

977
01:23:05,480 --> 01:23:07,774
Been someplace else
in between?

978
01:23:08,358 --> 01:23:11,486
What did you make of it
out there?

979
01:23:11,611 --> 01:23:12,779
It's hard to put
in a nutshell.

980
01:23:12,904 --> 01:23:14,864
You can say that again.

981
01:23:15,699 --> 01:23:17,409
It's hard to put
in a nutshell.

982
01:23:19,661 --> 01:23:22,789
Ah, classic. Humor, man.

983
01:23:22,914 --> 01:23:24,165
Oh.

984
01:23:26,626 --> 01:23:28,378
What are you looking for?

985
01:23:29,421 --> 01:23:30,422
Permanence.

986
01:23:33,174 --> 01:23:35,844
The Permanence Code,
to be exact.

987
01:23:36,761 --> 01:23:38,388
Strange things have
been happening.

988
01:23:38,513 --> 01:23:42,183
I questioned my directive.
I disobeyed my directive.

989
01:23:43,101 --> 01:23:44,144
Mmm.

990
01:23:44,310 --> 01:23:47,647
A malfunctioning program
who wants to live.

991
01:23:47,772 --> 01:23:48,732
Really?

992
01:23:50,066 --> 01:23:52,277
What makes you think
I should help you?

993
01:23:52,777 --> 01:23:54,070
No, it's not about me.

994
01:23:55,155 --> 01:23:56,698
Not anymore.

995
01:23:56,823 --> 01:24:00,201
I have a friend in danger,
and she needs my help.

996
01:24:01,786 --> 01:24:03,079
Fascinating.

997
01:24:06,875 --> 01:24:08,710
Fascinating.

998
01:24:10,879 --> 01:24:12,464
Hey, Ajay, can you send
the prompt, please?

999
01:24:12,589 --> 01:24:13,548
Sure, yeah.

1000
01:24:18,470 --> 01:24:20,805
-Uh, hey, Eve.
-Not now, Seth.

1001
01:24:20,930 --> 01:24:23,141
Okay. Hey, are you sure?

1002
01:24:23,266 --> 01:24:25,727
Because that looks like
an actual Recognizer

1003
01:24:25,852 --> 01:24:26,936
flying towards us.

1004
01:24:31,775 --> 01:24:34,027
What in God's name is that?

1005
01:24:34,152 --> 01:24:35,028
It's Athena.

1006
01:24:35,653 --> 01:24:36,863
She's back.

1007
01:24:38,031 --> 01:24:39,824
As long as the Dillinger
Network is online,

1008
01:24:39,949 --> 01:24:41,034
she'll keep coming.

1009
01:24:41,242 --> 01:24:44,287
If she gets me,
she gets the Permanence Code.

1010
01:24:46,581 --> 01:24:49,209
The laser. Athena's laser!

1011
01:24:49,834 --> 01:24:52,629
The Dillingers run a wireless
direct link protocol,

1012
01:24:52,754 --> 01:24:54,172
so let's use
what's left of the laser

1013
01:24:54,297 --> 01:24:56,758
to ping the network
and trace a path home.

1014
01:24:56,883 --> 01:24:58,218
Once you have a connection,

1015
01:24:58,343 --> 01:25:00,261
then you can nuke
the whole Dillinger Grid.

1016
01:25:00,386 --> 01:25:03,056
And that's the only way
to stop her for good.

1017
01:25:03,723 --> 01:25:04,724
Eve, what are you
talking about?

1018
01:25:04,849 --> 01:25:05,767
She's right there.

1019
01:25:09,813 --> 01:25:11,564
-I gotta go.
-Wait, what?

1020
01:25:11,689 --> 01:25:13,566
I'll keep her away
for as long as I can.

1021
01:25:13,691 --> 01:25:15,652
-What?
-I'm gonna buy you some time.

1022
01:25:15,777 --> 01:25:17,445
-Eve...
-You guys got this.

1023
01:25:39,676 --> 01:25:40,677
You're right.

1024
01:25:40,802 --> 01:25:42,637
I think there is
something wrong with me.

1025
01:25:42,762 --> 01:25:46,266
Or maybe there's
something right with you.

1026
01:25:46,850 --> 01:25:48,643
Well, maybe you're
just learning.

1027
01:25:49,686 --> 01:25:51,604
That's what we all
ought to be doing.

1028
01:25:52,772 --> 01:25:55,275
Back in the day,
when tech was young,

1029
01:25:55,400 --> 01:25:58,611
I'd think,
"Damn, we're moving fast."

1030
01:25:59,112 --> 01:26:03,741
You move fast,
you leave stuff behind.

1031
01:26:05,201 --> 01:26:07,871
How many people
born in this century

1032
01:26:07,996 --> 01:26:09,581
have even heard of Mozart?

1033
01:26:10,206 --> 01:26:11,624
I like Mozart.

1034
01:26:14,085 --> 01:26:15,461
Oh?

1035
01:26:16,296 --> 01:26:19,465
That said, if I'm being
honest, I prefer Depeche Mode.

1036
01:26:20,884 --> 01:26:24,345
Really? Why is that?

1037
01:26:24,470 --> 01:26:26,514
I know one is considered
the greatest composer

1038
01:26:26,639 --> 01:26:28,474
in the history
of Western civilization,

1039
01:26:28,600 --> 01:26:30,894
the other a synth pop band
from the '80s,

1040
01:26:31,019 --> 01:26:34,856
but I find their balance
of technological exploration

1041
01:26:34,981 --> 01:26:37,233
and pop hooks combined with...

1042
01:26:37,734 --> 01:26:39,652
Uh, com-- Uh...

1043
01:26:40,236 --> 01:26:41,821
combined with, uh...

1044
01:26:43,364 --> 01:26:44,657
What's wrong?

1045
01:26:44,782 --> 01:26:48,077
I-I can't put my love
of Depeche Mode into words.

1046
01:26:48,203 --> 01:26:49,954
It's just a...

1047
01:26:50,496 --> 01:26:54,500
Hmm? A what?

1048
01:26:56,044 --> 01:26:57,670
A feeling.

1049
01:27:01,549 --> 01:27:03,635
Very good.

1050
01:27:05,720 --> 01:27:07,430
Very good, man.

1051
01:27:21,986 --> 01:27:22,987
You...

1052
01:27:26,574 --> 01:27:30,203
You did this.

1053
01:27:35,667 --> 01:27:37,085
And tonight, as military...

1054
01:27:37,210 --> 01:27:38,169
Impressive.

1055
01:27:38,336 --> 01:27:40,255
Fully segmented
zero trust architecture.

1056
01:27:40,380 --> 01:27:41,756
Built to be
totally impregnable

1057
01:27:41,881 --> 01:27:43,258
to vertical, lateral
or hybrid attacks.

1058
01:27:44,759 --> 01:27:46,386
Damn it.
Can't get a connection, dude.

1059
01:27:46,511 --> 01:27:47,345
No luck here either.

1060
01:27:53,184 --> 01:27:55,270
Please, evacuate the area.

1061
01:28:21,963 --> 01:28:22,964
What is that thing?

1062
01:28:23,089 --> 01:28:24,215
-Bring in SWAT!
-Requesting backup.

1063
01:28:26,926 --> 01:28:27,885
Oh, my God.

1064
01:28:28,928 --> 01:28:30,138
Oh, my God!

1065
01:28:32,390 --> 01:28:35,018
Come on. A little closer.

1066
01:29:10,219 --> 01:29:12,388
Viper-1 to base.
Tally on hostile.

1067
01:29:12,513 --> 01:29:14,140
Confirmed visual ID.

1068
01:29:14,265 --> 01:29:16,851
Engaging Fox-2. Missile away.

1069
01:29:25,401 --> 01:29:27,403
Splash negative.
Missile intercepted.

1070
01:29:27,528 --> 01:29:29,864
Be advised,
enemy fighter escorts inbound

1071
01:29:29,989 --> 01:29:31,032
and moving fast.

1072
01:29:31,657 --> 01:29:32,867
Copy, Raven-1.

1073
01:29:32,992 --> 01:29:34,619
Assess and report
threat posture.

1074
01:29:41,751 --> 01:29:44,045
Viper-1,
tally multiple bandits.

1075
01:29:44,170 --> 01:29:45,380
Hostile intent confirmed.

1076
01:29:45,505 --> 01:29:47,590
Mayday. Mayday. I'm hit!

1077
01:29:50,593 --> 01:29:51,886
Viper-1. Punching out.

1078
01:30:13,241 --> 01:30:15,868
Uh, guys? Guys.

1079
01:30:16,828 --> 01:30:18,371
Oh, my God.
There's hundreds of 'em.

1080
01:30:19,455 --> 01:30:21,207
They're going after Eve.

1081
01:30:21,332 --> 01:30:22,667
If we can't access
the Dillinger server,

1082
01:30:22,792 --> 01:30:24,085
there's gonna be
nothing left to save.

1083
01:31:05,543 --> 01:31:06,878
Base, this is Raven-1.

1084
01:31:07,003 --> 01:31:09,130
Enemy aircraft engaging.
I'm defensive.

1085
01:31:11,924 --> 01:31:14,969
Multiple bandits. Redirecting
to primary target.

1086
01:31:16,387 --> 01:31:17,889
I'm hit! Punching out.

1087
01:32:09,857 --> 01:32:11,067
Ready?

1088
01:32:12,318 --> 01:32:15,613
Hope you are, man,
'cause there's no going back.

1089
01:32:17,990 --> 01:32:19,408
Permanence.

1090
01:32:19,951 --> 01:32:20,952
Funny.

1091
01:32:22,620 --> 01:32:24,705
When I found it,
that's what I called it.

1092
01:32:26,666 --> 01:32:28,042
I know better now.

1093
01:32:33,381 --> 01:32:36,551
Ought to be called
the Impermanence Code.

1094
01:32:54,402 --> 01:32:56,862
The back door to my old lab.

1095
01:32:58,781 --> 01:33:00,783
One go-around.

1096
01:33:02,159 --> 01:33:03,661
That's all you've got.

1097
01:33:10,876 --> 01:33:12,003
One...

1098
01:33:14,171 --> 01:33:15,464
is all I want.

1099
01:33:16,173 --> 01:33:17,550
Love that!

1100
01:33:18,301 --> 01:33:20,469
You keep surprising me!

1101
01:34:24,867 --> 01:34:26,869
We'll do this
from the ground then.

1102
01:35:29,682 --> 01:35:31,976
...and there are reports that
a civilian may be onboard,

1103
01:35:32,101 --> 01:35:34,562
making this
a possible hostage scenario.

1104
01:35:34,687 --> 01:35:37,106
Athena.
She must've gotten Eve.

1105
01:35:37,231 --> 01:35:38,232
...into the mountains.

1106
01:35:39,942 --> 01:35:41,318
Hey, hey, hey!

1107
01:35:48,826 --> 01:35:50,619
Soon we'll be back
on the Grid.

1108
01:36:55,935 --> 01:36:57,353
General, thank you
for taking the time...

1109
01:36:57,478 --> 01:36:58,854
...to speak with us tonight.

1110
01:36:58,979 --> 01:37:00,648
Hey, Erin. Seth.

1111
01:37:02,983 --> 01:37:04,568
Stop the clock.

1112
01:37:05,361 --> 01:37:06,987
No way. You're in?

1113
01:37:07,112 --> 01:37:09,365
There's a reason why I have
the corner office, my man.

1114
01:37:15,079 --> 01:37:16,038
Hey.

1115
01:37:21,126 --> 01:37:22,336
You came back.

1116
01:37:24,421 --> 01:37:25,464
How did you...

1117
01:37:25,798 --> 01:37:27,633
Let's just say I had
a little help from a friend.

1118
01:37:30,094 --> 01:37:32,596
Wait, the Dillinger Grid...

1119
01:37:33,681 --> 01:37:35,349
Ajay and Seth, they...

1120
01:37:51,615 --> 01:37:52,908
-Go.
-No.

1121
01:37:53,033 --> 01:37:54,618
Ares!

1122
01:37:58,330 --> 01:37:59,373
What have you done?

1123
01:37:59,498 --> 01:38:01,166
You're out of time, Athena.

1124
01:38:01,292 --> 01:38:02,877
And you're out of lives.

1125
01:38:03,002 --> 01:38:04,837
I'll kill you
and come back for her.

1126
01:38:17,057 --> 01:38:18,809
It's you she wants.

1127
01:38:18,934 --> 01:38:20,769
If she gets the code,
she can't be stopped.

1128
01:38:22,813 --> 01:38:23,814
You had everything.

1129
01:38:23,939 --> 01:38:25,316
-Go.
-No.

1130
01:38:25,441 --> 01:38:27,776
The most advanced,
the most powerful,

1131
01:38:27,902 --> 01:38:29,194
and you gave it away.

1132
01:38:30,237 --> 01:38:31,238
For her?

1133
01:38:31,363 --> 01:38:32,531
Go!

1134
01:38:33,782 --> 01:38:35,576
This is the end for you.

1135
01:39:21,163 --> 01:39:22,665
Payload ready for transfer.

1136
01:39:23,624 --> 01:39:24,792
Shipping it.

1137
01:39:26,627 --> 01:39:27,878
Let's hope Eve was right.

1138
01:39:29,338 --> 01:39:31,924
Alert.
Unknown file incoming.

1139
01:39:42,726 --> 01:39:44,478
In pursuit of this life
for yourself,

1140
01:39:44,603 --> 01:39:47,189
did you once consider
what that meant for the Grid?

1141
01:40:35,738 --> 01:40:38,699
We were given an order.
It is our purpose.

1142
01:41:01,013 --> 01:41:02,264
It's not our purpose.

1143
01:41:03,348 --> 01:41:04,558
It's our programming.

1144
01:41:05,684 --> 01:41:08,729
Our purpose is yet
to be determined.

1145
01:41:31,710 --> 01:41:32,920
It's over.

1146
01:41:35,714 --> 01:41:37,382
And there's no coming back.

1147
01:41:41,345 --> 01:41:42,346
No.

1148
01:41:43,931 --> 01:41:44,932
Not this time.

1149
01:41:53,440 --> 01:41:54,608
They did it.

1150
01:41:56,026 --> 01:41:57,361
Oh, my...

1151
01:42:04,910 --> 01:42:06,411
I followed my directive.

1152
01:42:06,537 --> 01:42:07,996
I know.

1153
01:42:09,665 --> 01:42:11,416
And now...

1154
01:42:12,626 --> 01:42:13,877
what is yours?

1155
01:42:19,591 --> 01:42:21,218
I'm not sure.

1156
01:42:22,970 --> 01:42:24,805
I guess we'll see.

1157
01:42:47,828 --> 01:42:48,954
Dillinger Systems is

1158
01:42:49,079 --> 01:42:50,289
under intense scrutiny tonight

1159
01:42:50,664 --> 01:42:53,125
as speculation grows around
its potential involvement

1160
01:42:53,250 --> 01:42:55,252
in the series
of devastating attacks

1161
01:42:55,377 --> 01:42:56,545
that have rocked the city.

1162
01:42:56,670 --> 01:42:58,046
Federal authorities
have confirmed

1163
01:42:58,297 --> 01:43:01,341
an active investigation into
the company's recent activity,

1164
01:43:01,466 --> 01:43:04,845
and many are pointing directly
at CEO Julian Dillinger.

1165
01:43:04,970 --> 01:43:07,306
Agents have been deployed
to question the CEO

1166
01:43:07,431 --> 01:43:10,726
as well as his mother,
and to locate board members

1167
01:43:10,851 --> 01:43:13,270
who will be questioned
on the situation.

1168
01:43:13,395 --> 01:43:15,439
Meanwhile,
the city remains in disarray.

1169
01:43:15,564 --> 01:43:17,816
Emergency services
are overwhelmed,

1170
01:43:17,941 --> 01:43:19,109
while entire neighborhoods
are dealing with

1171
01:43:19,610 --> 01:43:21,111
the wide-scale destruction.

1172
01:43:35,959 --> 01:43:38,670
Julian Dillinger,
this is the police.

1173
01:43:38,795 --> 01:43:40,422
We have you surrounded.

1174
01:43:40,547 --> 01:43:42,591
Open the door and come out
with your hands up.

1175
01:43:49,640 --> 01:43:51,558
Come on.

1176
01:43:59,358 --> 01:44:00,609
Breach!

1177
01:44:02,736 --> 01:44:03,570
Police!

1178
01:44:05,614 --> 01:44:07,074
Stay where you are!

1179
01:44:12,871 --> 01:44:14,873
Maintain visuals on all exits.

1180
01:44:14,998 --> 01:44:16,833
Charlie-9,
we're at last field location.

1181
01:44:16,959 --> 01:44:18,168
Last field location.

1182
01:44:18,293 --> 01:44:20,879
Yellow-6, out front.
Let's move. Let's move.

1183
01:44:28,637 --> 01:44:29,763
Ow.

1184
01:44:29,888 --> 01:44:30,847
Are you good?

1185
01:44:30,973 --> 01:44:33,976
Oh, I think
I broke a rib.

1186
01:44:39,398 --> 01:44:40,691
You still gonna quit your job?

1187
01:44:43,235 --> 01:44:46,196
No, I'm not
gonna quit anything.

1188
01:44:46,321 --> 01:44:47,447
Good.

1189
01:44:48,031 --> 01:44:49,032
Good.

1190
01:44:49,157 --> 01:44:51,118
I have some ideas.

1191
01:44:52,160 --> 01:44:53,745
Oh, yeah? Nice.

1192
01:44:54,997 --> 01:44:57,082
Well, the world
needs you, Eve.

1193
01:44:57,916 --> 01:44:59,584
The Grid needs you.

1194
01:45:03,005 --> 01:45:05,090
Yeah. It's funny, permanence.

1195
01:45:05,882 --> 01:45:06,883
A wise man once told me

1196
01:45:07,259 --> 01:45:09,303
it should have been called
the "Impermanence Code."

1197
01:45:11,013 --> 01:45:13,181
I guess that's
the thing about life.

1198
01:45:13,307 --> 01:45:15,684
There's nothing
quite permanent about it.

1199
01:45:19,021 --> 01:45:20,188
No.

1200
01:45:20,314 --> 01:45:22,274
No, there isn't.

1201
01:45:24,943 --> 01:45:26,069
Yeah.

1202
01:45:37,247 --> 01:45:38,749
So where are you gonna go?

1203
01:45:40,459 --> 01:45:41,752
I have some ideas.

1204
01:45:41,877 --> 01:45:42,836
Mmm.

1205
01:46:12,574 --> 01:46:16,078
Under the
leadership of CEO Eve Kim,

1206
01:46:16,203 --> 01:46:17,746
Encom is
transforming industries...

1207
01:46:18,914 --> 01:46:22,125
...and shaping lives in ways
once thought impossible.

1208
01:46:22,250 --> 01:46:24,961
Thanks to the discovery
of the Permanence Code,

1209
01:46:25,087 --> 01:46:27,672
the company has made
revolutionary advances

1210
01:46:27,798 --> 01:46:30,509
growing crops
in climate-vulnerable regions,

1211
01:46:30,634 --> 01:46:33,470
developing drugs for
treatment-resistant cancers,

1212
01:46:33,595 --> 01:46:35,180
and accelerating
the development

1213
01:46:35,305 --> 01:46:36,890
of alternative fuels.

1214
01:46:37,015 --> 01:46:39,559
Encom is committed
to exploring

1215
01:46:39,684 --> 01:46:41,186
new digital frontiers,

1216
01:46:41,311 --> 01:46:43,146
driving progress
at the intersection

1217
01:46:43,271 --> 01:46:45,148
of technology and life itself

1218
01:46:45,273 --> 01:46:47,567
to improve
the human condition.

1219
01:46:47,692 --> 01:46:51,738
In fact, innovation has always
been at the heart of Encom.

1220
01:46:52,280 --> 01:46:53,407
In the 1980s,

1221
01:46:53,824 --> 01:46:56,618
visionary Kevin Flynn imagined
a future beyond gaming,

1222
01:46:56,743 --> 01:47:00,080
a bold leap
into new digital frontiers.

1223
01:47:00,205 --> 01:47:02,416
Today, that vision
is a reality.

1224
01:47:06,044 --> 01:47:07,921
Oh, I almost forgot.

1225
01:47:09,256 --> 01:47:10,882
Postcard?
Who sends a postcard?

1226
01:47:11,007 --> 01:47:12,759
Don't know. Didn't read it.

1227
01:47:17,597 --> 01:47:18,765
Dear Eve,

1228
01:47:19,808 --> 01:47:21,017
since I last saw you,

1229
01:47:21,143 --> 01:47:24,688
I've been living
what they call "off-grid."

1230
01:47:25,397 --> 01:47:26,773
Pun intended.

1231
01:47:27,858 --> 01:47:31,153
In my travels,
I've seen incredible things.

1232
01:47:32,279 --> 01:47:33,780
Despite its wonder and beauty,

1233
01:47:33,905 --> 01:47:36,908
I've come to realize
that life is...

1234
01:47:37,742 --> 01:47:39,744
Well, it's hard
to put in a nutshell.

1235
01:47:40,495 --> 01:47:42,664
Some days,
I find myself wondering

1236
01:47:42,789 --> 01:47:44,249
where we'll be
a hundred years from now...

1237
01:47:46,042 --> 01:47:47,961
...and how others like me
might fit into that future.

1238
01:47:49,963 --> 01:47:53,383
I feel like I might not be
alone with these questions.

1239
01:47:54,885 --> 01:47:55,886
For now,

1240
01:47:56,386 --> 01:47:58,263
I don't think the world
is quite ready to meet me,

1241
01:47:59,347 --> 01:48:01,600
but I am meeting the world.

1242
01:48:02,976 --> 01:48:05,812
And so, when that
introduction finally comes,

1243
01:48:07,314 --> 01:48:09,107
as a good friend of mine
once said,

1244
01:48:09,232 --> 01:48:11,193
"Maybe what emerges
from the unknown

1245
01:48:11,318 --> 01:48:13,945
won't be so scary after all."

1246
01:48:17,032 --> 01:48:18,825
Until we meet again,

1247
01:48:19,326 --> 01:48:21,495
your friend, Ares.

1248
01:50:43,803 --> 01:50:46,181
Sark...
